==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|advocacie}}, {{m|enm|advocacye}}, {{m|enm|advocatye}}, from {{der|en|frm|advocacie}}, {{m|frm|advocatie}}, {{m|frm|avocacie}} and {{der|en|ML.|advocātia}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|advocate|acy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæd.və.kə.si/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-advocacy.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{a|Philippines}} {{IPA|en|/æd.ˈvoʊ.kə.si/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
{{wikipedia}}

# The [[profession]] of an [[advocate]].
# The act of [[arguing]] in [[favour]] of, or [[supporting]] someone or something.
# The practice of supporting someone to make their voice heard.

